{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex","id":668932,"title":"Role Playing the fall of Pentex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-17T16:04:07-07:00","id":668932,"title":"Role Playing the fall of Pentex","content":"In the Settite Clanbook, there is a Rite to destroy entire organizations by ritually killing the head of that organization in the same manner that Set killed Osiris. Incidentally it only works on males. Say that the CEO of Pentex is caught, and a jillion successes are achieved on the Rite. The next day the corporate stock goes down to pennies and every board member and manager in Pentex has been the exposed as unintentional guest stars on &quot;To Catch a Predator.&quot;. Or something to that affect. What would the worldwide demise of Pentex look like? After its assets get auctioned off and its employees laid off, and the politicians have to whore themselves out to new donors, what changes and what is the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:07:57-07:00","id":668951,"title":"","content":"Well, they'd probably push the button that causes all their owned nuclear reactors to explode, because if they're going down, they're taking as many of you with them as they can.<br /> <br /> Of course, not to dick around players, but it would be completely reasonable to say the rite can't work in the case you describe, because the real head of Pentex is not the CEO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:13:33-07:00","id":668954,"title":"","content":"That rite sounds like the most absurdly anti-climactic way to de-rail a story ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:40:38-07:00","id":668965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=668954#post668954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That rite sounds like the most absurdly anti-climactic way to de-rail a story ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically, they are probably warded to high hell by the Nephandi. The real quest would be taking down the Death Star's many layers of mystic shields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:07:00-07:00","id":669053,"title":"","content":"Why the hell would the followers of set even try to take down pentex? Who would they teach the rite to out side of clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:03:31-07:00","id":669131,"title":"","content":"Well, there was that one Inconnu in Layer of the Hidden.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, don't forget about the Serpents of Light and the possibility of them coming to the conclusion that Pentex is a tool of the Antis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-17-2015, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:39:33-07:00","id":669146,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I just have to shake my head at what you post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T22:07:28-07:00","id":669249,"title":"","content":"The possibility is very remote, but is not beyond a lot of other unlikely scenarios that I see come up. Besides, this thread was more about the aftermath of the demise of Pentex then about the means of its destruction. So if Pentex goes belly up then how does the world change?<br /> <br /> Edit: Besides, that one Setite Inconnu along with The Serpents of Light show that the Clan can't be sure that it's secrets aren't going to wind up in the wrong hands. I also seem to remember that Koldunic's spread through out the Sabbat was also an extremely unlikely scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-18-2015, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T03:42:40-07:00","id":669435,"title":"","content":"The world does not change if you destroy Pentex. It's the same messed up hell, just with millions more desperate people without jobs and critical infrastructure shortages. Pentex is but one of many heads of the Hydra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:36:04-07:00","id":670009,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Pentex is in some ways a joke: a small handful of Captain Planet villains whose efforts are a drop in the ocean compared to what billions of mundane humans do to their own planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:47:27-07:00","id":670037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=670009#post670009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Pentex is in some ways a joke: a small handful of Captain Planet villains whose efforts are a drop in the ocean compared to what billions of mundane humans do to their own planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: Okay, cutting the sarcasm and Archer references. In the game, Pentex has been structured according to a very real world corporate greed model since at least Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition, which stands in stark contrast to Captain Planet villains, who are all basically bizarre Mage characters. Who else would make so many plans revolving around bizarre gadgets like shrink rays and mind-switching machines but an Etherite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-18-2015, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:03:41-07:00","id":670956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=669435#post669435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world does not change if you destroy Pentex. It's the same messed up hell, just with millions more desperate people without jobs and critical infrastructure shortages. Pentex is but one of many heads of the Hydra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vehemently disagree. Sure, the world isn't going to magically fix itself. The Wyrm still has a lot of hooks left to cling to.<br /> However, the disintegration of Pentex has three direct results:<br /> 1) The overarching plans break down. Anything that has corporations cooperate for the end game (aka the Apocalypse) rather than act for their own benefit doesn't work anymore because there's noone left to force them to do so.<br /> 2) Financing the Wyrm's plans gets a lot harder. While there are some servants of the Wyrm that can get their hands on money, many of the slime-and-tentacle faction need someone to handle their finances and get a little money together because most mundane banks think &quot;buy up some square kilometres in the middle of nowhere because there's a site sacred to Mother Nature there&quot; is not a solid business model to grant a loan for.<br /> 3) Industrial Fomori production winds way down. Project Iliad is a pure money-sink that only pays for itself as long as you have other operations that can benefit from Fomori forces. And without Project Iliad, you've only got &quot;naturally&quot; occurring Fomori and some small-scale production left in the world. Garou losses would probably decrease significantly.<br /> <br /> @Dwight<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why the hell would the followers of set even try to take down pentex? Who would they teach the rite to out side of clan? </div> </div> </div>Who knows? Maybe one of Pentex' excavation teams accidentally dug up the burial site of a Setite Methusaleh who got reduced to ashes in the process. Maybe the Serpents got a good look at some of Pentex' end game scenarios and decided it's not the kind of Apocalypse they'd like happen. It's not something that would automatically occur, but it's hardly impossible.<br /> Additionally, there are several breeds of Changers that make a habit of stealing wyrmish lore and at least one of those has a longstanding enmity against the Setites anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> @Topic<br /> Essentially, you'd get a feeding frenzy where all factions would try to make a grab for as many pieces of the corpse as they can. More benevolent actors would try to cushion the economical and infrastructural impact, mundane buyers try to get rich (and would likely become corrupted by their acquisitions, thus forming miniature versions of the old Pentex) and Wyrm minions would try to acquire the pieces of the whole that let them continue their own plans with as little interruption as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:23:45-07:00","id":670982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=670956#post670956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vehemently disagree. Sure, the world isn't going to magically fix itself. The Wyrm still has a lot of hooks left to cling to.<br /> However, the disintegration of Pentex has three direct results:<br /> 1) The overarching plans break down. Anything that has corporations cooperate for the end game (aka the Apocalypse) rather than act for their own benefit doesn't work anymore because there's noone left to force them to do so.<br /> 2) Financing the Wyrm's plans gets a lot harder. While there are some servants of the Wyrm that can get their hands on money, many of the slime-and-tentacle faction need someone to handle their finances and get a little money together because most mundane banks think &quot;buy up some square kilometres in the middle of nowhere because there's a site sacred to Mother Nature there&quot; is not a solid business model to grant a loan for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately for a lot of caerns, there tend to be notable quantities of valuable natural resources present, so point number two isn't quite a certainty. At the very least, threats from logging and mining subsidiaries will remain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Industrial Fomori production winds way down. Project Iliad is a pure money-sink that only pays for itself as long as you have other operations that can benefit from Fomori forces. And without Project Iliad, you've only got &quot;naturally&quot; occurring Fomori and some small-scale production left in the world. Garou losses would probably decrease significantly. </div> </div> </div>You can't really count on that, either, since someone, somewhere, will try it at least once. This is the WoD, and most people don't actually know how fomori work; they're even labeled &quot;nutritional supplement users&quot; on any records that people might see. The only way it stops all of the sudden is if you want to incorporate an influential Technocracy into your game, and they start testing the alleged nutritional supplements and subjects up close, in a proximity which SPD did not allow. They'd freak out pretty quickly if they found out that all of this was just a front for putting &quot;extradimensional entities&quot; into people; the mad dash to put a stop to it and potential for shootouts and crossfires between groups would be sublime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who knows? Maybe one of Pentex' excavation teams accidentally dug up the burial site of a Setite Methusaleh who got reduced to ashes in the process. Maybe the Serpents got a good look at some of Pentex' end game scenarios and decided it's not the kind of Apocalypse they'd like happen. It's not something that would automatically occur, but it's hardly impossible.<br /> Additionally, there are several breeds of Changers that make a habit of stealing wyrmish lore and at least one of those has a longstanding enmity against the Setites anyway. </div> </div> </div>Speaking of stealing lore, I picked up a copy of DB: Bone Flowers recently, and it had an odd mechanic in it wherein Cainite necromancy rituals could be adapted for use as rites by Hungry Dead (short story - add one to the level of the V:tM ritual). Given that the mechanics of Gui Ren rites are set up similarly to Garou and Fera rites, it would probably be possible to crib the ritual. Of course, the adapted Cainite rituals are also reviled by the elders as heretical and possibly/likely corrupting, so there's that to deal with, but the Eaters of the Dead are already in for a pound or more just by practicing their signature rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:01:35-07:00","id":671004,"title":"","content":"@Saur Ops Specialist<br /> Of course, none of these things is a 100% shiny-daisies-and-fluffly-puppies world saver. However, it's a matter of degrees. Human greed results in some benefit for the Wyrm, but the real deal gets done when someone goes beyond simple greed and acts purely to serve the Wyrm, hoping for rewards not by way of the bottom line, but by an ageless entity of corruption. Sure, Caerns may have natural ressources, but there are still some more such places left in the world. And if I've got four possible sites including one where three logging companies have already gone and utterly failed before, I know which one I strike off the list as long as I'm just in it for the money.<br /> As for Fomori: Sure, there will always be Fomori, possibly even intentionally fabricated ones. But there's a difference in scale between a single craftsman discovering the entire process for themself and an industrial complex refining their methods over decades. I don't see anyone else creating Fomarchs, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:18:17-07:00","id":671017,"title":"","content":"also it would be mean less people are infested with bane spirits because they ate burgers at O'toolys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:39:36-07:00","id":671034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=671017#post671017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also it would be mean less people are infested with bane spirits because they ate burgers at O'toolys</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the bane spirits would still be around. The game doesn't do the &quot;evil spirits in every last thing of modern manufacture&quot; bit any more. Instead, it's like The Jungle, and sometimes long pork accidentally gets processed into the burgers, making them unsuspectingly more susceptible to possession by banes that can only possess individuals who have engaged in cannibalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:43:54-07:00","id":671035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=671034#post671034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the bane spirits would still be around. The game doesn't do the &quot;evil spirits in every last thing of modern manufacture&quot; bit any more. Instead, it's like The Jungle, and sometimes long pork accidentally gets processed into the burgers, making them unsuspectingly more susceptible to possession by banes that can only possess individuals who have engaged in cannibalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they got rid of the companies of Pentex that actually stuff burgers with Bane spirits and have it that you get bane spirits from watching tv?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:20:47-07:00","id":671049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=671035#post671035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they got rid of the companies of Pentex that actually stuff burgers with Bane spirits and have it that you get bane spirits from watching tv?</div> </div> </div> </div>A long time ago. Products can be made in a way to piss spirits off or draw their attention, but the fall of Starburst Computers described in the Tellus chapter of Subsidiaries made it clear that items that actually have banes in them don't sell very well, and W20 made for a nice time to retcon all of the &quot;bane in a box&quot; stuff into &quot;box makes banes mad if they are present&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:14:40-07:00","id":671506,"title":"","content":"Am curious, what would happen to leftover Formori, mockery breed members, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:24:57-07:00","id":671514,"title":"","content":"Some are put down before the lights go out, some die when noone opens their cages, some are coopted by other factions, some escape into the wild. I guess that about covers the options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:39:37-07:00","id":671530,"title":"","content":"I would never let players do this to Pentex. Not only is it anti-climactic and anti-thematic, but Pentex is backed by such powerful spirits that even an Antediluvian would be unlikely to overcome them. <br /> <br /> Also, Pentex is such a major corporation (or conglomeration of corporations) that the idea of it dying doesn't make sense economically or industrially. Pentax doesn't just exist as words on paper - there are factories all over the world, stores, distribution centers, products, land holdings, and so on. Those things don't disappear because some executives die. At the very most, the leadership could collapse and cause Pentex to split into numerous smaller companies, each influenced by the Wyrm in different ways and to different degrees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:59:10-07:00","id":671548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=671530#post671530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would never let players do this to Pentex. Not only is it anti-climactic and anti-thematic, but Pentex is backed by such powerful spirits that even an Antediluvian would be unlikely to overcome them.<br /> <br /> Also, Pentex is such a major corporation (or conglomeration of corporations) that the idea of it dying doesn't make sense economically or industrially. Pentax doesn't just exist as words on paper - there are factories all over the world, stores, distribution centers, products, land holdings, and so on. Those things don't disappear because some executives die. At the very most, the leadership could collapse and cause Pentex to split into numerous smaller companies, each influenced by the Wyrm in different ways and to different degrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex was just a corp once - it would be a serious loss, but a far from fatal one. Sooner or later another mogul or ambitious mid-level will bite and things start all over again. In fact Pentex fall could make things <b>worse</b> in the long run, as several subsidiary execs see an opportunity to make their own business empires using their supernatural edges against several other businesses that have little to no defense or preparation in that area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:18:10-07:00","id":671570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact Pentex fall could make things <b>worse</b> in the long run, as several subsidiary execs see an opportunity to make their own business empires using their supernatural edges against several other businesses that have little to no defense or preparation in that area. </div> </div> </div>I would assume this is exactly what happens right now, no downfall necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:17:23-07:00","id":671824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/668932-role-playing-the-fall-of-pentex?p=671570#post671570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume this is exactly what happens right now, no downfall necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly - Pentex is huge but one mamooth empire can be sometimes slow moving as it must balance all its many (some already considerable) parts as it advances on anything, not to mention its sheer size collaborates for many an ambitious mid-exec to focus in internal advancement and backstabbing <b>amongst those already part of that world</b> on some level, instead of pouncing upon the wider mostly defenseless business world around it.<br /> <br /> Pentex organizes and directs, but it also restrains up to a level for the sake of internal coherence and stability, what can also curtail overall efficiency on a number of spots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:03:43-07:00","id":672157,"title":"","content":"This scenario reminds me of the climax of Angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T23:22:07-07:00","id":672947,"title":"","content":"Actually just destroying Pentex would have horrifying consequences to the world at large. For all the shit they do and for all the evil of their agenda, they are still the world's biggest corporation incorporating endless subsidiaries. Most of these subsidiaries are staples of the community, huge employers, have a solid public image (no worse then any other corp) and actually offer key services. Just imagine what might happen if Endron's power plants were taken out or if Magadon's medicine supplies started shorting out.<br /> <br /> Pentex falling means that all of this would be gone. We are talking about millions of people suddenly going out of a job all over the world and giant vacuums appearing in large segments of the world's industry and business. The destruction of Pentex would drive countless employees into desperation, apathy, panic and chaos. Even while they would have been &quot;good&quot; and untainted, the life they would be living would make them the perfect breeding ground for a new army of fomori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T09:58:55-07:00","id":675336,"title":"","content":"Pentex as written is a perfect example of a company that is too big to fail. About 13 years ago a major energy company was found to be playing with its books. The resulting crash of one stock was enough to cause a recession. The latest recession and economic slump was caused by a number of factors but a key was the collapse of one company Lehman brothers. If Pentex falls the Apocalypse instead of being stopped might be accelerated. Asmodai above mentioned a number of good points. Short of a hostile takeover by a Weaver aligned company that stabilizes the company the fall of Pentex just might be enough to trigger a worldwide economic collapse that devastates the entire global economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:57:53-07:00","id":675569,"title":"","content":"Pentex being too big to fail is also the reason given as to why The Technocracy hasn't taken it out...<br /> Though if we could get some Firebrand Socialists in the NWO to get some ideas... ...<br /> <br /> Glass Walker/NWO Buddy Cop Show. It is known.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:26:41-07:00","id":675952,"title":"","content":"could you give a name/page number on the Rite? I'm having a real hard time finding it and would like to see the wording because it seems to me it would be reasonable that the Rite just enhances the natural tendencies of the Company members to backstab and scatter, Pentex doesn't officially exist as a super mega conglomerate so it would be pretty easy to scale things down to each of the subsidaries","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T18:18:20-07:00","id":683674,"title":"","content":"I Think its unthemantic for Pentex to be unkillable.<br /> <br /> And yes destroying it WOULD mean millions unemployed... but I dont think that is worse then the corpoations continued existence... in fact I think &quot;Birth pangs&quot; Of a new and better future is appropiate<br /> <br /> speaking of which... why is the omega plan not mentioned in anniversary book of the wyrm?<br /> <br /> or the black spiral 3 creeds, of Power, Cunning, and Infamy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}